'''Killun Station''' was a station operated by the [[Imperial Security Bureau]], a part of the [[Galactic Empire]], located on [[Killun 71]].<ref name="DAD" />

==Description==
Killun Station was an [[Imperial Security Bureau]] outpost built onto one of the misty moon [[Killun 71]]'s jagged landmasses. Since it held sensitive data including Imperial clearance codes, the station was tightly guarded. [[Stormtrooper]]s were posted at all entrances and all visiting personnel and [[droid]]s had to pass through [[walkthrough identification scanner]]s.<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|killun-station|Killun Station}}</ref>

==History==
In [[2 BBY]], Killun Station was breached by the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|rebel]] [[droid]]s [[AP-5]] and [[C1-10P|Chopper]] during a [[Mission to recover Imperial codes|mission]] to steal clearance codes for the [[Phoenix Cell]]'s upcoming raid on [[Lothal]]. While AP-5 managed to steal the clearance codes from the [[Central Computer Core]], Chopper was remotely reprogammed by a team of Imperial intelligence officers led by [[Boon|LT-319]], who was based aboard an [[IGV-55 surveillance vessel]].<ref name="DAD" />

==Behind the scenes==
Killun Station first appeared in the ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]'' [[Star Wars Rebels Season Three|Season Three]] episode "[[Double Agent Droid]],"<ref name="DAD" /> which premiered on [[Disney XD]] on [[March 11]], [[2017]].<ref name="TV.com">{{TVcom|url=shows/star-wars-rebels/double-agent-droid-3447914|text=Star Wars Rebels - Season 3, Episode 18: Double Agent Droid}}</ref>

